+# Incident Triage Playbook — RT / HIL / Perception failures (ScoutAV)
+
+Purpose
+- Rapid, repeatable triage process for hardware RT SLO failures, HIL critical failures, and perception long-tail regressions.
+
+Immediate actions (first 30 minutes)
+1) Identify failure type (RT / HIL / Perception)
+   - RT: check rt_slo_proof.json for p99_ok / safe_ok false
+   - HIL: review campaign_summary.json and waveform_compare.json
+   - Perception: review /perception/ood_results.json and failures.json
+
+2) Capture & secure evidence
+   - Copy bundle path (from operator run outputs) and upload to secure S3 evidence bucket
+   - Ensure cosign signatures and Rekor entries (if available) are recorded
+
+3) Notify stakeholders (Slack / Pager)
+   - Controls Lead (controls-lead@example.com)
+   - Safety Officer (safety-officer@example.com)
+   - Perception Lead (perception-lead@example.com)
+   - Infra Operator (infra@example.com)
+
+4) Attach artifacts to triage issue
+   - Required artifacts:
+     - rt_slo_proof.json (for RT)
+     - campaign_summary.json, measured.ndjson, waveform_compare.json (for HIL)
+     - failures.json, adv_data.ndjson (for Perception)
+     - evidence manifest (evidence_manifest.json)
+   - Create GH issue using template: title prefixed "URGENT TRIAGE: <domain> - <short summary>"
+
+Root cause checklists
+- RT
+  - CPU isolation missing? (check /etc/aegis-runner-labels, cset output)
+  - IRQ affinity on NICs? (check /proc/irq/*/smp_affinity_list)
+  - PREEMPT_RT kernel? (uname -v)
+  - Logging overload / disk IO spikes? (iostat, dmesg)
+
+- HIL
+  - Scenario runner errors? (check HIL logs and measured.ndjson)
+  - Waveform mismatch: review compare logs and check golden trace alignment
+  - Timing drift between test harness and controller (NTP/ptp)
+
+- Perception
+  - Environment mismatch (sim vs real): inspect scenario metadata
+  - Sensor calibration & timestamp alignment
+  - NPU runtime failures: check vendor runtime logs on NPU runners
+
+Mitigation & rollback
+- If issue is critical safety (e.g., safe-stop miss), immediately put fleet into restricted mode (geofence/stop) and initiate rollback:
+  - Use canary rollback manager: ops/av/ops/canary_rollout_manager.py to revert to previous manifest
+  - Notify certifier/auditor if running certified fleet
+
+Post-incident
+- Conduct RCA, produce timeline, update test matrix & scenarios, add new tests to HIL campaign, and re-run validation.
+- Update evidence bundle and re-submit to certifier if applicable.
+
